speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, we have made the kind of progress I had hoped we would have made by today. I also feel reasonably confident that we can complete our work tomorrow. I therefore suggest that we defer any further consideration of Bill C-52 and third reading of Bill C-69 until tomorrow. I therefore move, seconded by the Minister of Public Works (Mr. Drury):
That the House shall sit on Saturday, December 20, 1975;
And that, for the purposes of Standing Orders 2, 6 and 15, that sitting shall be deemed to be a Friday, except no private members business shall be taken up.
